  "summary": "The dissertation experimentally implements a discrete‑time quantum walk using a Bose–Einstein condensate of 87Rb atoms, where microwave pulses act as the coin and an atom‑optics kicked‑rotor ratchet performs the shift. The system demonstrates quantum‑walk momentum spreading (σ ≈ j vs classical σ ≈ √j) and experimental control features such as biased walks, reversals, and quantum‑to‑classical transition, with experiments performed for up to about 20 walk steps and kick strengths |k| = 1.2–1.8.",
